Cases expected GREEN before the Implementer, on purpose: the nested-path case (`/settings/life-areas/unknown` is
`today` today as well) and `taskIdFromRoute("life-areas")` (null at runtime) — they pin the paths the new line sits on, so
a prefix-match implementation of the route fails them after Task 3. Every pre-existing app-route case stays green.

New-case count: about 88 (life-areas-list 47, life-areas-view 33, app-route 8; it.each rows counted individually).

Names, shapes and copy taken from the plan rather than the PRD (PRD AC-19 is manual and names no function): the two
modules' exports and signatures, the state kinds `loading` / `ready { areas, noAreaOpenTaskCount }` / `failed { message }`,
the event types `loaded` / `load-failed` / `created` / `renamed` / `deleted`, `LifeAreaNameProblem`
(`blank` | `too_long` | `duplicate`), and every pt-BR sentence pinned verbatim — each is fixed in Task 1 or Task 2's ACTION
and in the plan's Notes ("For the test pair"). No wording the plan leaves to the Implementer is pinned.

Assertions that go beyond the literal PRD text, each taken from the plan or from a risk it names, so R-IMPL-LEAK can judge
them:
- `loaded` returns a COPY: the response array handed in is not reordered (plan Task 1 "a COPY ... sorted");
- the reducer does not mutate a frozen ready state for created, renamed and deleted (the useReducer contract; plan Task 1
  mirrors google-settings.ts, whose reducer is pure the same way);
- `created` is idempotent by id and never zeroes the counts of an area a refetch already brought in (plan Risks row 2);
- `renamed` keeps the three counts because PATCH answers none, and `deleted` adds `openTaskCount`, never `taskCount`, to
  Sem área (plan Task 1 and Risks rows 3 and 4);
- a delete or rename of an id the list does not hold changes nothing, so a repeated event cannot double-count (plan
  Task 1 "only when an area has that id");
- an accent-only or case-only rename is NOT a no-op and is sent (plan Task 1 item 6: only an exact no-op is skipped);
- renaming an area to its own name in another case is accepted by checkLifeAreaName, while another area's name is still a
  duplicate (plan Task 1 item 5; PRD AC-4 "casa" case);
- the server's own error text, which carries a tool-facing field marker such as `(name)`, never reaches the owner (plan
  Task 2 last sentences; decision 2 in the plan's Notes).

Not encoded as tests, by the PRD's own TDD routing and the methodology's scope: the visual and interaction clauses listed
under "Manual clauses", the glossary-vocabulary scan and the sibling-only-imports scan (both are Level 2 shell checks in the
plan, not test files) and the four client wrappers in src/app/api.ts (src/app is outside the test project).

